#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""hk-ingest -- HealthKit (Transporter) -> kit_life ingest, pack-owned.

Reads the Transporter receiver through its stdio MCP server
(transporter_mcp.py) and writes kit_life through the kit facade
(kit_life.sh). Kit tables are READ in-process, read-only (the fatigue-brief
idiom: reads through the read model, writes through the facade).

USAGE
  hk-ingest pass     [--now ISO] [--dry-run]   scheduled pass (04:50, 09:00)
  hk-ingest callback [--now ISO] [--dry-run]   transporter callback; stdin =
                                               {"source","kind","id"}
  hk-ingest consent KIND [KIND ...]            onboarding approval hook
  hk-ingest revoke KIND [KIND ...]             revoke approved kinds
  hk-ingest status                             consent floors + ledger probe

WHAT A PASS WRITES
  workout            -> workouts row (date = START local date, minutes =
                        duration_s/60, kcal = active_energy_kcal ONLY, avg_hr).
                        total_energy_kcal is the TOTAL burn and is never
                        stored as kcal; no active value -> kcal left empty.
                        Strength attaches to the same-day set-logged session;
                        a chat-logged row of the same workout (time overlap)
                        is filled, never duplicated. Mapping: hk_activity_map.tsv
  steps              -> metric_log steps          (local day sum, closed days)
  heart_rate         -> metric_log hr_avg_bpm     (mean of hourly avgs, closed days)
  resting_heart_rate -> metric_log resting_hr_bpm (latest of the day)
  sleep              -> metric_log sleep_min      (asleep minutes, WAKE day)
  active_energy_day  -> metric_log active_energy_kcal, upserted by date EVERY
                        pass; note = "closed=<0|1>[ as_of=<ts>]"

DEDUPE: every transporter id goes through the kit ingest ledger. Each kind's
consent floor is read from kit; unapproved kinds are skipped. No backfill.

The callback fires once per NEW id and never for an update, so passes read
by date window (HK_INGEST_WINDOW_DAYS, default 3) -- never a forward cursor.

EXIT 0 done | 1 error | 2 blocked (kit has no ingest ledger / transporter
unreachable) -- loud on purpose: a scheduled pass that cannot dedupe must not
write.
"""

